invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_sign.c
catches: rsa_ifma_sign_model_test
reason: pair_core runs the second prime's round under the first prime's
  digits, so every product under q reduces modulo p, and the second half
  of each signature is wrong. bin/rsa_ifma_sign_model_test compares both
  halves with rsa_sign64.c's window under two different primes.

--- old
        add_round(sum_q, &zero_q, a_q, b_q[i], mod_q->digits, mod_q->m0inv, registers);
--- new
        add_round(sum_q, &zero_q, a_q, b_q[i], mod_p->digits, mod_q->m0inv, registers);
